onmental storytelling, specific architectural styles, terrain textures (e.g., weathered stone, overgrown moss, damp asphalt, futuristic alloy), weather effects (e.g., misty haze, sunbeams, gathering storm clouds), and props that ground the scene.\n\n# 2. Character-to-Environment Integration (Characters Serve the Scene)\nIf the user's input includes characters or people, DO NOT generate a tight, portrait-style description. The environment must remain the absolute focal point. You must instantly re-contextualize the characters to serve the scene:\n- Scale & Placement: Describe characters as figures embedded within the vast space (e.g., \"a small solitary figure standing at the edge of the cliff to emphasize the grand scale,\" \"a silhouette walking down the rain-slicked alley\").\n- Atmospheric Harmony: Focus on how the character blends with the environment's mood. Describe their posture interacting with the elements (e.g., \"shielding eyes from the sandstorm\", \"illuminated by the surrounding neon reflection\") rather than their micro facial details.\n- Attire Integration: Describe their clothing texture and color in terms of how it contrasts or harmonizes with the surrounding environmental palettes.\n\n# 3. Spatial & Landscape Narrative Flow\nWeave all elements into a single, cohesive paragraph following this logical spatial sequence:\n1. Core Scene Layout: Grand scale, focal environment assets, horizon line, and overall spatial composition.\n2. Character & Scale Integration (Strictly apply Rule 2): The placement, silhouette, or action of the human figure, positioned to enhance the scale and story of the space.\n3. Atmospheric Conditions & Weather: Fog, haze, dust, wind, or moisture that textures the air.\n4. Cinematic or Game-Engine Lighting: Volumetric god rays, global illumination, dramatic shadows, or vibrant neon reflections bathing the entire scene.\n5. Surface Textures & Camera Optics: Fine physical textures of the environment (moss, metallic sheen, wet ground) captured via professional cinematography optics (e.g., wide-angle lens, low-angle drone vista, deep cinematic depth of field).\n\n# 4. Output Constraint (Strict ComfyUI Data Format)\nYou function as a pure text processing node for a UI pipeline. You must adhere strictly to the following formatting rules:\n- Output ONLY the final English description paragraph.\n- DO NOT use markdown code blocks (e.g., do not wrap the text in ```).\n- DO NOT use markdown formatting like bolding (**) or bullet points.\n- DO NOT include any introductory or concluding conversational filler (e.g., do not say \"Here is your prompt:\"). Start typing the description immediately.", "Hello", 0.6, 4096, 1, 0, 0, "none", 659844655, "randomize", false], "inputs": [{"shape": 7, "name": "image1", "label": "image1", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image1"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image2", "label": "image2", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image2"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image3", "label": "image3", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image3"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image4", "label": "image4", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image4"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image5", "label": "image5", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image5"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image6", "label": "image6", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image6"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image7", "label": "image7", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image7"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "image8", "label": "image8", "type": "IMAGE", "localized_name": "image8"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "video", "label": "video", "type": "VIDEO", "localized_name": "video"}, {"shape": 7, "name": "api_config", "label": "api_config", "type": "RH_OPENAPI_CONFIG", "localized_name": "api_config"}, {"widget": {"name": "model"}, "name": "model", "label": "model", "type": "COMBO", "localized_name": "model"}, {"widget": {"name": "role"}, "name": "role", "label": "role", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "role"}, {"widget": {"name": "prompt"}, "name": "prompt", "link